        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 85-year-old male patient, admitted on 22/04/2013 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, clinical examination revealed significant dyspnoea, prolonged expiration, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation without signs of pneumonia. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests were unremarkable for infection. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and intravenous fluids for hydration. Continuous pulse oximetry monitoring was performed throughout the stay. The patient responded well to treatment with notable symptomatic improvement. He was discharged on 23/04/2013 with an optimised inhaler regimen and patient education regarding disease self-management. Please arrange follow-up within two weeks.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
